{"name":"Magic Fountain","hex":"#1f75ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"magic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The application of rituals or actions, especially those based on occult knowledge, to subdue or manipulate natural or supernatural beings and forces in order to have some benefit from them. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The supernatural forces which are drawn on in such a ritual."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having supernatural talents, properties or qualities attributed to magic.","Producing extraordinary results, as though through the use of magic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic"},{"term":"fountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A natural source of water; a spring.","An artificial, usually ornamental, water feature (usually in a garden or public place) consisting of one or more streams of water originating from a statue or other structure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flow or gush as if from a fountain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fountain"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Magic Fountain (opera)","blocks":[{"text":"The Magic Fountain is a three-act lyric drama, the second opera by the English composer Frederick Delius. The libretto by the composer was inspired by the legend of the fountain of eternal youth recounted by Juan Ponce de León, and the work is set in Florida and the Everglades at the time of the Spanish conquest."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Magic_Fountain_(opera)","wikidata":"Q137591316"},{"title":"The Magic Fountain","blocks":[{"text":"The Magic Fountain is a 1961 film starring Peter Nestler and Helmo Kindermann."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Magic_Fountain","wikidata":"Q7749426"},{"title":"Magic Fountain (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Magic Fountain is the second extended play by Australian electronic band Art vs. Science. It was released on 14 July 2010."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4a/Magic_fountain_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_Fountain_(EP)","wikidata":"Q6730696"},{"title":"Fountain","blocks":[{"text":"A fountain, from the Latin \"fons\", meaning source or spring, is a decorative reservoir used for discharging water. It is also a structure that jets water into the air for a decorative or dramatic effect in landscapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Fountains_Collage.jpg/330px-Fountains_Collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain","wikidata":"Q483453"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG/500px-Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG/1280px-Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG/500px-Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Egyptian fountain on the Temple of Dendera","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADendera_Tempel_19.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Fish_fountain_in_Hotel_Du_Caumont_Aix.jpg/500px-Fish_fountain_in_Hotel_Du_Caumont_Aix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Fish_fountain_in_Hotel_Du_Caumont_Aix.jpg/1280px-Fish_fountain_in_Hotel_Du_Caumont_Aix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Fish_fountain_in_Hotel_Du_Caumont_Aix.jpg/500px-Fish_founta